# Kute: served in place of the game's clouds_0.obj (774 KB of cloud geometry).
# Blocking that request outright is what this client used to do, and the game then draws its cloud pass with a
# program that never linked, which logs "useProgram: program not valid" every frame. A valid model keeps the
# render path whole, and one triangle a thousandth of a unit across is nothing to draw.
o kute_empty_clouds
v 0.000000 0.000000 0.000000
v 0.001000 0.000000 0.000000
v 0.000000 0.001000 0.000000
vn 0.000000 1.000000 0.000000
vt 0.000000 0.000000
vt 1.000000 0.000000
vt 0.000000 1.000000
f 1/1/1 2/2/1 3/3/1
